@startuml diagrama_implantacao
'============================================================
' DIAGRAMA DE IMPLANTACAO
' Fase 1 (prototipo standalone) e Fase 2 (plugin VST3/AU)
' Cobre PB30 - portabilidade de formatos
'============================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #2F4858
skinparam nodeBorderColor #2F4858
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF6D9
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9A227

title Diagrama de Implantacao\nFase 1: aplicacao Python standalone | Fase 2: plugin nativo dentro da DAW

'============================================================
' FASE 1
'============================================================
node "**FASE 1 - Maquina de desenvolvimento**" <<device>> #EEF4FB {

  node "Sistema Operacional\n(Windows / macOS / Linux)" as OS1 {

    node "Runtime Python 3.11+" <<executionEnvironment>> as PYRT {
      artifact "main.py" as A_MAIN
      artifact "eq/dsp/*.py\n(NumPy + SciPy)" as A_DSP
      artifact "eq/io/audio_io.py\n(sounddevice)" as A_IO
      artifact "eq/ui/*.py\n(Tkinter + Matplotlib)" as A_UI
      artifact "presets/*.json" as A_JSON
    }

    node "Driver de audio\nWASAPI / CoreAudio / ALSA" as DRV1
  }
}

node "Interface de audio\n(placa / mic)" <<device>> as HW1 #FFFFFF

A_MAIN --> A_UI
A_UI --> A_DSP
A_IO --> A_DSP
A_IO --> DRV1 : PortAudio
DRV1 --> HW1
A_DSP --> A_JSON : salva / carrega

note bottom of PYRT
  Executavel standalone para validacao
  matematica e de resposta de sinal.
  Sofre com o GIL: a UI e o audio
  disputam o mesmo interpretador, por isso
  esta fase nao tem compromisso de latencia.
end note

'============================================================
' FASE 2
'============================================================
node "**FASE 2 - Maquina do usuario final**" <<device>> #EAF6EE {

  node "Sistema Operacional" as OS2 {

    node "DAW Host\n(Reaper / Ableton / Logic / FL)" <<executionEnvironment>> as DAW {

      component "Thread de audio da DAW" as T_AUDIO
      component "Message Thread da DAW" as T_UI

      artifact "**SelvaEQ.vst3**\nPluginProcessor + DSP" as A_VST3
      artifact "**SelvaEQ.component**\n(AU - somente macOS)" as A_AU
      artifact "libjuce (estatica)" as A_JUCE
    }

    node "Driver de audio\nASIO / CoreAudio / WASAPI" as DRV2
    folder "Pasta de presets do usuario\n~/Documents/SelvaEQ/*.xml" as FS2
  }
}

node "Interface de audio profissional" <<device>> as HW2 #FFFFFF

T_AUDIO --> A_VST3 : processBlock()
T_UI --> A_VST3 : APVTS
A_VST3 --> A_JUCE
A_AU --> A_JUCE
DAW --> DRV2
DRV2 --> HW2
A_VST3 --> FS2 : presets XML

note bottom of DAW
  PB30: um unico codigo-fonte JUCE gera
  VST3 e AU. O plugin nao possui processo
  proprio: roda dentro do processo do host,
  por isso qualquer bloqueio na Audio Thread
  vira glitch audivel em toda a sessao.
end note

'============================================================
' MIGRACAO
'============================================================
A_DSP -[#9B59B6,dashed]-> A_VST3 : PB30 - matematica validada\nem Python e traduzida para C++
A_JSON -[#9B59B6,dashed]-> FS2 : conversao de formato\nJSON -> XML (APVTS)

'============================================================
' AMBIENTE DE BUILD
'============================================================
node "Ambiente de build / CI" <<device>> #F7F7F7 {
  artifact "CMake + JUCE 7" as BUILD
  artifact "pluginval\n(validacao automatizada)" as PVAL
  artifact "pytest\n(testes do motor Python)" as PYTEST
}

BUILD --> A_VST3 : compila
BUILD --> A_AU : compila
PVAL --> A_VST3 : valida (PB17)
PYTEST --> A_DSP : valida coeficientes\ncontra scipy.signal

@enduml
